lls (technical), negatives: can be grumpy, uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). So strengths in reliability, stress, technical, but concerns in cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), known 100% reliable (reliability), creates positive atmosphere with crew (crew cooperation), but difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (team), not willing to further education (adaptability). So strong reliability, decision, crew, but communication and adaptability concerns.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but regarded as arrogant (crew cooperation, communication), relatively weak leadership (crew), also arrogant may affect crew. So strengths in technical, responsibility, attention, but concerns in cooperation.\n\nWe need to compare. Which candidate best overall? Candidate C has reliability, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has reliability, stress, technical, but uncooperative. Candidate A has strong technical and leadership but unorganized and poor at criticism. Candidate D strong technical and responsibility but arrogance.\n\nProbably Candidate C seems strongest on reliability and crew, but communication issues could be safety-critical. Candidate B also strong but uncooperative. Might need more info on crew cooperation for B and D. We could ask other panel members for more details on Candidate B's crew cooperation and communication, and Candidate C's communication difficulty specifics.\n\nThus initial contribution: share summary and propose provisional vote for Candidate C, but note concerns and request info on communication and adaptability. Provide METADATA vote.\n\nLet's do that."}
